    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 90376,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90376.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 7,
    "turn_text": "It was really an extraordinary call. It's actually the second time that I've met with President Zelensky. What I saw in this Zoom conference was really the extraordinary leader, a gentleman who had no political experience, but understood the dynamics of leadership. To address a nation and crisis, it was really important to see him in his element. a man of great courage. He knows that he's the first person that the Russians are going to eliminate. And he actually talked about a mayor that had been executed as just a way of introducing us to the risk that the political leadership in Ukraine has. But he's standing firmly and has rallied the people of Ukraine and really rallied the people of the world to Ukraine's side in this horrible invasion that Putin has thrust upon his country.",
