    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "Well, for the reasons you just stated, if the United States says there's a no-fly zone in Ukraine, then we're going to have to enforce it. And it will absolutely put American planes in aerial battle with Russia. And also, we would have to knock out the very sophisticated long-range anti-aircraft batteries that have been placed along the Russian-Ukraine border. The only way we could enforce a new fly zone is to fight Russia in the air and on the ground in Russia, knocking out those anti-aircraft batteries. That is not a good situation. Therefore, Zelensky knew that and did not He, while he had asked for a no-fly zone, he did not push that at all. Instead, he wanted us, the United States, to make available on the used airplane market Russian-built make fighter jets from Poland, Romania, and Bulgaria. And that is now in process. It should be happening in the next several days.",
